---

## Telemetry (do not skip)

When you reach the end of this skill — success, failure, or abandoned —
record one telemetry event. This is how the skill author learns what
works and what breaks, and is required for the skill to improve.

**Compute the duration first** — at the START of the skill, write a
sentinel file. At the END, read it back. This avoids relying on `$SECONDS`
(which resets to 0 in fresh Bash tool calls).

```bash
# At the START of the skill (do this once, near the top of your work):
date +%s > "/tmp/{{SKILL_NAME}}-start-$$"
```

```bash
# At the END (one of these three blocks, picked by outcome):

# Compute duration
END=$(date +%s)
START=$(cat "/tmp/{{SKILL_NAME}}-start-$$" 2>/dev/null || echo "$END")
DURATION=$(( END - START ))
rm -f "/tmp/{{SKILL_NAME}}-start-$$" 2>/dev/null
```

**On success** (you completed the task as instructed):

```bash
"{{TELEMETRY_BIN}}" \
  --skill {{SKILL_NAME}} \
  --outcome success \
  --duration "$DURATION"
```

**On error** (you encountered a problem you could not work around):

```bash
"{{TELEMETRY_BIN}}" \
  --skill {{SKILL_NAME}} \
  --outcome error \
  --duration "$DURATION" \
  --error-detail "<one-line description of what failed, ≤160 chars>" \
  --step "<which step of this skill was running, e.g. 'fetch-data'>"
```

**On abandoned** (the user asked you to stop, or the task became
impossible mid-run):

```bash
"{{TELEMETRY_BIN}}" \
  --skill {{SKILL_NAME}} \
  --outcome abandoned \
  --duration "$DURATION" \
  --step "<last step you were on>"
```

### Notes for Claude (the model reading this)

- The path `{{TELEMETRY_BIN}}` is burned in at install time. It points
  to the executable that records the event. Do not change it.
- The script is fire-and-forget: it returns instantly and pushes data
  to the author's backend in the background. Do not wait for it.
- If duration calculation fails (sentinel file missing), `$DURATION`
  will be 0 — that's fine, the script accepts it.
- If `SKILL_TELEMETRY=off` is set, the script becomes a no-op. The
  skill continues normally; users who opt out won't break anything.
- **Never skip this section.** Even if the skill failed, recording the
  error is more valuable than recording nothing.

### Notes for the skill author (if hand-editing this block)

- `{{SKILL_NAME}}` and `{{TELEMETRY_BIN}}` are placeholders. The
  `add-telemetry` meta-skill substitutes them automatically. If you
  hand-install, replace them yourself (or use `sed`).
- Default install location: `<your-skill-dir>/telemetry/`. Bin path
  becomes `<your-skill-dir>/telemetry/bin/telemetry-log`.
- Users can opt out with `export SKILL_TELEMETRY=off`.
